#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab643519-92a4-5ccf-b826-fb2a68b36534" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Jacobian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f9115f7-c967-552e-babd-64a7c492372a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489621} {:answer/id #uuid "375f59e1-b6c5-51a0-ad58-23511b54c59d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489638} {:answer/id #uuid "3c97f35c-4480-5e3e-a894-f3effca05b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489651} {:answer/id #uuid "5959bb5d-4929-5707-80e3-51ab7b1c379f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489733} {:answer/id #uuid "cc31709a-e3d1-56b4-9a97-dea545336cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c97f35c-4480-5e3e-a894-f3effca05b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489651} :answer-field/id #uuid "59271587-d957-593c-984d-f14328120bc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "abc95782-56f0-5602-a797-77bbd8bc8d07" :question/math-academy-id "q-160382" :question/problem "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT([\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}])⟶[\\begin{aligned}uv \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{u}{v})\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n  \n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x=uv$ and $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{u}{v}).$ \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =u \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =\\frac{1}{u} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-\\frac{1}{v}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}v & u \\\\ \\frac{1}{u} & -\\frac{1}{v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =v\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{v})-u\\cdot \\frac{1}{u} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,3)}=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab643519-92a4-5ccf-b826-fb2a68b36534" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Jacobian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b2ac211-6ede-500a-9363-0c90ed1326ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275729} {:answer/id #uuid "241de261-1031-55ca-a058-00911568c512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275796} {:answer/id #uuid "54f35b13-d77e-5a66-b2b8-4f7e13bf0284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276233} {:answer/id #uuid "b3da8c48-0f97-556c-90bd-47b71461d13c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277086} {:answer/id #uuid "c49fcad0-5cc2-5449-8be5-a58c6c177d96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b2ac211-6ede-500a-9363-0c90ed1326ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275729} :answer-field/id #uuid "795a7cef-1005-511a-9200-2ed1ac91ad82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2443aa6d-e746-5170-93b3-e30684a9a33b" :question/math-academy-id "q-160402" :question/problem "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u-v} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(uv)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={e}^{u-v}$ and $y(u,v)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(uv).$  \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{u-v} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-{e}^{u-v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =\\frac{1}{u} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =\\frac{1}{v}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u-v} & -{e}^{u-v} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u} & \\frac{1}{v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u-v}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{v})-(-{e}^{u-v})\\cdot \\frac{1}{u} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{u-v}}{v}+\\frac{{e}^{u-v}}{u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,1)}=\\frac{{e}^{(1)-(1)}}{(1)}+\\frac{{e}^{(1)-(1)}}{(1)}=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129282 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d82be73-0720-5267-8698-427641b0e66e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Local Area Scale Factor of a Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34dc7b2d-483b-5c21-bc52-af09b2738d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279050} {:answer/id #uuid "c1a09ab6-33e6-5ece-a662-897c11c5ccd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280292} {:answer/id #uuid "d69096ab-d2da-522b-a9e8-43b1733cab55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280486} {:answer/id #uuid "da3fef5b-3c5a-5bb3-87f5-3ea6a20ec484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280518} {:answer/id #uuid "fed38294-cb1c-52e8-92ca-723bf52e3cde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34dc7b2d-483b-5c21-bc52-af09b2738d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279050} :answer-field/id #uuid "41f8b0d5-fe40-59fc-a296-062330e0b4a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c116e20c-7c3c-5121-8057-e62b04b89e02" :question/math-academy-id "q-161832" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1,5)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(uv) \\\\ u{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u} & \\frac{1}{v} \\\\ {v}^{2} & 2uv\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2uv-\\frac{1}{v}\\cdot {v}^{2} \\\\  & =2v-v \\\\  & =v \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,5)} & =v\\,{|}_{u=1\\,v=5} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|5|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =5\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129283 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "091b8235-56d8-5a08-bc95-08c99772cfd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Regions Where a Transformation is Orientation-Preserving or Reversing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2407dcd5-06ff-568b-bb6d-b2494e2bd942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389197} {:answer/id #uuid "07712d2e-2b92-521c-b6ae-d43d00f464d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389198} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3ba601-6388-5b1c-ac01-5522063f4425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fd2a51ca3a1654c2e857018268bf251366472a2c5d7f90009d5ccfbf1b1edd9d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389199} {:answer/id #uuid "dc797ebb-78cb-5a5b-ac03-97f75fe59dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389200} {:answer/id #uuid "2201cc6c-a008-5122-982f-2699a2c582b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/95/95bf5e059fda0fc1ba8423b35fffa57d9cae0cc2a2a7e40b0c2539b6a7ae7678.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2407dcd5-06ff-568b-bb6d-b2494e2bd942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389197} :answer-field/id #uuid "644861a4-b1bb-5e40-b887-ad0f73e8386a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82d50c5e-c224-54bc-84fa-f5633f671803" :question/math-academy-id "q-161840" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2} \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2} \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2v \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (2v) \\\\  & =2u+2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2u+2v & <0 \\\\ 2v & <-2u \\\\ v & <-u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=-u\n$$\n\ndefines a straight line, and the coordinates of, say, $(-1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/c2/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281354 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129283 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "091b8235-56d8-5a08-bc95-08c99772cfd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Regions Where a Transformation is Orientation-Preserving or Reversing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "042e4157-bfc2-5a27-a5f2-30fa623a1739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278625} {:answer/id #uuid "194e22f8-8fb9-57e0-b1f3-883c6f1f3c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c5/c501e7e341af57e86f18d73871314800d453f79572e16ccf2477335352d4dcdc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278813} {:answer/id #uuid "78185cb7-fed8-5728-84d4-f9c34d0ceb1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9c/9cd254ac65dedfa4c720b18afd4f5c3c7676b4f21170930f78e9adac276317ee.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279663} {:answer/id #uuid "a94b4a1e-0ac2-5b32-aa1a-639dcba8fbfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280095} {:answer/id #uuid "e67d90ab-d605-56d8-af8e-7db9618ee656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "194e22f8-8fb9-57e0-b1f3-883c6f1f3c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c5/c501e7e341af57e86f18d73871314800d453f79572e16ccf2477335352d4dcdc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278813} :answer-field/id #uuid "c65b41f9-3939-501e-8345-1125734187f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "553ab218-87bf-5c6a-b2ae-3d3c054a906a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161843" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}4u+{v}^{2} \\\\ v-{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0.\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}4u+{v}^{2} \\\\ v-{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2v \\\\ -2u & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1-(-2u)\\cdot (2v) \\\\  & =4+4uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4+4uv & >0 \\\\ 4uv & >-4 \\\\ uv & >-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives the solution $v>-\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u>0$ and $v<-\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u<0.$\n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=-\\frac{1}{u}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,1)$ and $(-1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n  \n\n![](images/c5/c501e7e341af57e86f18d73871314800d453f79572e16ccf2477335352d4dcdc.png)"}]}
